[24.145, "o", "\r\nHere's a comprehensive breakdown of the slowest queries in your database:\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🐢 Slowest Queries — Full Report\r\n\r\n### 📊 By Total Database Time Impact\r\n\r\n| # | Query Summary | Calls | Total Time | Mean Time | Max Time | Cache Hit | Disk Reads | % of DB Time |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 1 | `audit_log` — COUNT by table/action with time filter | 5 | 389.55ms | 77.91ms | 270.83ms | 80.07% | 8,572 | **30.36%** |\r\n| 2 | `audit_log` — JSONB `new_values` status aggregation | 5 | 253.95ms | 50.79ms | 65.42ms | 98.93% | 480 | **19.79%** |\r\n| 3 | `orders` — EXTRACT() date filter | 5 | 134.58ms | 26.92ms | 31.11ms | 100% | 0 | **10.49%** |\r\n| 4 | `order_items` ⨝ `products` — lookup by order_id | **250** | 132.50ms | 0.53ms | 2.83ms | 83.81% | 633 | **10.33%** |\r\n| 5 | `orders` ⨝ `customers` — filter by shipping (col truncated) | 5 | 124.64ms | 24.93ms | 26.13ms | 99.54% | 29 | **9.71%** |\r\n| 6 | `orders` ⨝ `customers` — filter by status + date range | 5 | 92.97ms | 18.59"]
[0.000, "o", "ms | 19.19ms | 80.57% | 1,232 | **7.24%** |\r\n| 7 | `customers` ⨝ `orders` — revenue by country | 5 | 85.30ms | 17.06ms | 18.68ms | 99.93% | 4 | **6.65%** |\r\n| 8 | `audit_log` — IN subquery on orders status | 5 | 69.77ms | 13.95ms | 44.37ms | 98.24% | 323 | **5.44%** |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🔍 Key Findings & Red Flags\r\n\r\n### 🚨 #1 — `audit_log` COUNT/GROUP BY with time filter *(30.36% of all DB time!)*\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT count(*), table_name, action\r\nFROM audit_log\r\nWHERE changed_at > NOW() - interval $1\r\nGROUP BY table_name, action\r\nORDER BY count(*) DESC\r\n```\r\n- **Cache hit only 80.07%** with **8,572 disk reads** — the worst offender by far.\r\n- Likely doing a **full sequential scan** on `audit_log` with no index on `changed_at`.\r\n- **Recommendation:** `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY ON audit_log (changed_at);`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### ⚠️ #2 — `audit_log` JSONB aggregation *(19.79% of DB time)*\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT new_values->>'status' AS new_status, count(*) AS change_count\r\nFROM audit_log\r\nWHERE action = $2 AND table_n"]
[0.000, "o", "ame = $3\r\nGROUP BY ...\r\n```\r\n- Returns **208,335 rows** — very large result set being aggregated.\r\n- Cache hit is good (98.93%), but the sheer volume of data processed is the issue.\r\n- **Recommendation:** `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY ON audit_log (action, table_name);`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### ⚠️ #3 — `orders` with `EXTRACT()` date filter *(10.49% of DB time)*\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT id, order_date, total_amount\r\nFROM orders\r\nWHERE EXTRACT(year FROM order_date) = $2\r\n  AND EXTRACT(month FROM order_date) = $4\r\n```\r\n- **`EXTRACT()` wrapping a column prevents index usage** — even if `order_date` is indexed, this forces a sequential scan.\r\n- **Recommendation:** Rewrite using a range filter:\r\n  ```sql\r\n  WHERE order_date >= '2024-01-01' AND order_date < '2024-02-01'\r\n  ```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### ⚠️ #4 — `order_items` ⨝ `products` lookup *(N+1 Pattern Risk!)*\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT oi.quantity, oi.unit_price, p.name, p.category\r\nFROM order_items oi\r\nJOIN products p ON p.id = oi.product_id\r\nWHERE oi.order_id = $1\r\n```\r\n- Called **250 "]
[0.000, "o", "times** — far more than any other query. Classic **N+1 pattern** (one call per order).\r\n- Each call is fast (0.53ms avg), but **633 disk reads** accumulate across all calls.\r\n- **Recommendation:** Investigate whether the application can batch these lookups.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### ⚠️ #6 — `orders` status + date range filter *(7.24% of DB time)*\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT o.id, o.total_amount, c.full_name\r\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c ON o.customer_id = c.id\r\nWHERE o.status = $1 AND o.order_date > NOW() - interval ...\r\n```\r\n- **80.57% cache hit** with **1,232 disk reads** — suggests a missing composite index.\r\n- **Recommendation:** `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY ON orders (status, order_date);`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 Priority Action Plan\r\n\r\n| Priority | Action | Expected Impact |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| 🔴 **P1** | Index `audit_log(changed_at)` | Eliminate 8,572 disk reads, fix 30% of DB time |\r\n| 🔴 **P1** | Index `audit_log(action, table_name)` | Fix 19.79% of DB time |\r\n| 🟠 **P2** | Rewrite `EXTRACT()` query to use range fi"]
[0.000, "o", "lter | Enable index usage on `orders.order_date` |\r\n| 🟠 **P2** | Index `orders(status, order_date)` | Fix disk reads on status+date queries |\r\n| 🟡 **P3** | Investigate N+1 on `order_items` lookup | Reduce 250 repeated calls |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWould you like me to **deep-dive into any specific query** with `EXPLAIN ANALYZE`, check the **table stats** for `audit_log` or `orders`, or proceed with **creating the recommended indexes**?"]
