[0.001, "o", "\r\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\r\n  ⚠️  REMEDIATION APPROVAL REQUIRED\r\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\r\n\r\n  The agent wants to execute the following:\r\n\r\n  Action 1:\r\n    SQL:    CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_orders_status_order_date ON orders (status, order_date)\r\n    Reason: The query filtering orders by status AND order_date currently uses idx_orders_status (single column), which fetches 20,000 rows by status and then discards 18,472 of them via a post-filter on order_date. This wastes significant I/O. A composite index on (status, order_date) allows PostgreSQL to satisfy both predicates at the index level, returning only the ~1,528 matching rows directly. This query accounts for 7.24% of total DB time with 1,"]
